From: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: Uke SSC: allow repeated mount-matrix coefficients

A mount matrix has positional entries and legitimately repeats zero and one.
The generic string-array type requires unique values. Use its non-unique
counterpart for this property only, retaining the nine-element cardinality
and acceleration-only admission. Do not change the matrix data or other
string-array properties.

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/xiaomi,uke-ssc-sensors.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/xiaomi,uke-ssc-sensors.yaml
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
         description: Alternative registry model names; no fitted identity claim.
       mount-matrix:
         description: Rotation from firmware-reported acceleration to the native panel axes.
-        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string-array
+        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/non-unique-string-array
         minItems: 9
         maxItems: 9
     allOf:
